    "description_stripped": "This record is the shared reader-facing home for modern LaTeX working materials for SGA 1, SGA 5, and SGA 6. It contains bounded English translations, French source/workpass readers, a bounded Spanish SGA 6 tranche, editable source, and source/build/render audit evidence.\n\nReader first: the 309-page SGA 5 English source-synchronized working edition remains the default preview. Its curated scope is Exposes I, III, III B, V, VI, VII, VIII, X, XII, and XV through printed page 480 plus the index through printed page 484. The page-14 source defect and page-43 ambiguity remain explicitly disclosed.\n\nSGA 1: the bounded six-page English checkpoint covers the Expose I heading/opening through section I.3, corrected French authority lines 556-799. Section I.4 at line 800 is next. Its exact evidence package contains editable TeX, public source/formula/structure/normalization/adverse-choice ledgers, build records, all six page renders, original-print adjudication, continuation cursor, caveats, and manifests.\n\nSGA 6: the French source-rescribe workpass reaches index 684 / printed page 671. The 377-page layered English reader promotes source reconciliation for index 663-684. Earlier material remains layered rather than uniformly page-audited; index 685-702 and terminal matter remain scan-checked working text pending later French reconciliation. The bounded Spanish Expose X index 532-537 tranche remains available.\n\nPublic-surface remediation: this version removes an obsolete 2026-07-06 SGA 5 support archive after a privacy audit found host-local path and workflow material. It also removes two stale 2026-07-17 CSV controls that refer only to absent superseded files. The current compact SGA 5 replacement and current SGA 6 idx684 reader/evidence package remain byte-identical. Historical published versions remain part of immutable Zenodo version history.\n\nStatus: these are machine-assisted working editions, translations, source-rescribe checkpoints, and audit artifacts. They are not complete SGA volumes, official or critical editions, peer review, proof certification, independent human or native-language certification, rights determinations, uniform whole-volume source certification, accessibility-tagged editions, or guarantees that every symbol and translation choice is correct. Bounded source-audit claims apply only to their stated ranges.\n\nGitHub: corrections and reproducible improvements can be proposed at https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts.",
    "version": "2026-07-18 SGA1 through I.3; SGA5/6 current objects retained; legacy support remediated",
